    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d716">

                <pb facs="0532" n="528" xml:id="pg528"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1115/3794: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Japan</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Grew</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Tokyo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1938-11-06T11:00:00+09:00">November 6, 1938—11
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 6—7 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Our 706, November 5, 2 p.m.,<anchor n="38" xml:id="d716-f1"/> reference Kuling
                    situation. The Foreign Office states that instructions were sent yesterday to
                    the Japanese naval and military authorities at Kiukiang to consult with American
                    and British Commanders with a view to rendering assistance.</p>
                <p>Sent to Hankow, repeated to Chungking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Grew</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
